= Preparing the Pie

Prepare @./pie-dough{2}.

Line a pie pan as described in the pie dough recipe, but do not bake.

Prepare the other dough by rolling to 1/8 inch thick and 14 inches in diameter, chill with lined pan.

Preheat oven to 425°F.

Whisk @granulated sugar{110%grams}, @cornstarch{57%grams}, @lemon zest{1}, and @salt{} in a #big mixing bowl{}.

Toss @frozen fruit{850%grams} with the dry ingredients.

Add fruit to lined pie pan, then place other prepared dough over the top, trim the edges with scissors and crimp together with your fingers to seal.

Cut some slits in the top crust.

= Baking

Use the lowest rack.

Place pie on a #sheet pan{} and into the oven, bake for ~{20%minutes}, rotating after 10 minutes.

> Anytime you rotate, assume 180 deg.

Drop the temperature to 375°F and continue baking for ~{30%minutes}.

Remove pie and cover crust with aluminum foil, place back in oven, rotate from previous position.

Cook another ~{30%minutes}, then remove and cover the whole pie with foil (loosely), place back in oven and rotate.

Cook for the last ~{30%minutes} covered.

Remove from oven and cool.
